{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507279378,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDY5NTM1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1871#issuecomment-334695359"},"message":"If anything then this is a documentation issue. In order to report the `author` value in the `metadata` value of a result dict one could simply say `--output-format '{metadata[author]}`.\n\nLearn your Python, Michael....\n\nBut it seems more complicated for fields that have a vocabulary prefix:\n\n```sh\n% datalad --output-format '{metadata[name]}' search score --max-nresults 1\n[INFO   ] Query completed in 0.00144505500793 sec. Reporting max. 1 top match. \nGhost Love Score\n% datalad --output-format '{metadata[music:genre]}' search score\n[INFO   ] Query completed in 0.00165200233459 sec. Reporting max. 20 top matches. \n[ERROR  ] Missing ']' in format string [base.py:\u003clambda\u003e:405] (ValueError) \n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507279559,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDY5NjAwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1871#issuecomment-334696000"},"message":"Jup. From https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#format-string-syntax\n\n\u003e Because arg_name is not quote-delimited, it is not possible to specify arbitrary dictionary keys (e.g., the strings '10' or ':-]') within a format string. \n\nToo bad...\n\nShould we change the prefix separator? But that wouldn't fix the issue ion general.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1507285652,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDcxODI1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1871#issuecomment-334718258"},"message":"Well, it's just about that `arg_name` we use for `format`, not about the actual names of the fields, right?\nSo it should be doa